{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether the petitioners\u2019 argument would be the same if, after a denial of class certification in one West Virginia district, the same plaintiff filed the identical complaint in another district and sought certification again."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg questioned whether simply obtaining a new named plaintiff would satisfy the requirements for a class action."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan inquired whether a federal Rule\u202f23 decision can ever be preclusive with respect to a state Rule\u202f23."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan also asked whether Congress, when enacting the Class Action Fairness Act, contemplated the issue of a lawyer filing in different states with different named plaintiffs."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer queried whether there is any precedent of a plaintiff seeking class certification in a different federal court after a denial in another court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether a subsequent plaintiff who was not given notice or an opportunity to opt out would be bound by a prior denial of class certification, even if the later filing is in the same court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan noted that the case was dismissed because a summary\u2011judgment motion was granted, not because of the denial of class certification."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia observed that a party attempting to bring a later class action cannot do so because a prior class action was denied."
      }
    ],
