  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners emphasized that they received no notice or opportunity to be heard regarding the denial of class certification, raising due\u2011process concerns."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, monahan argued that West Virginia\u2019s Rule\u202f23 may be applied independently of the federal rule and must be interpreted consistent with state procedural rights."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument Summary",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue they were not named plaintiffs in the prior federal proceeding and never received notice, an opportunity to be heard, to opt out, or to appeal the denial of class certification."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners assert that procedural rights, including due process, must be adjudicated consistently and that West Virginia may apply and interpret its own Rule\u202f23 as it sees fit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MR. MONAHAN",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MR. MONAHAN, monahan states that the Court has recognized a procedural right to seek class certification, but there is no substantive right to obtain it."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MR. BECK",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MR. BECK, beck frames the core issue as whether absent class members can be bound by a denial of class certification when there was adequate representation on the issue but no notice or opportunity to be heard."
      }
    ],
