              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners were not named plaintiffs in the prior proceeding and never received notice, an opportunity to be heard, to opt out, or to appeal the denial of class certification."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-13fa1aa15811-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 7,
                "start": 7
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, procedural rights must be adjudicated consistent with due process, and West Virginia may apply and interpret its own Rule\u202f23 as it sees fit."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. MONAHAN",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. MONAHAN, there is no substantive right to class certification; only a procedural right to seek it."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. MONAHAN",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. MONAHAN, the recent Thorogood case from the Seventh Circuit may be a relevant precedent."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. BECK",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "13fa1aa1581158f10c6da4a73e741103b93e974e09312a7c6b9c36f2d5f30d10",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-13fa1aa15811-0001-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. BECK, the core issue is whether absent class members can be bound by a denial of class certification when there was adequate representation but no notice or opportunity to be heard."
        }
      ],
